\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Cumulative price levels of the core and satellite assets, rebased to 100 at February 2004. Shaded regions mark the three crisis episodes inside the sample. Final index values are annotated at the right of each panel. XLK (Technology, 1471) and XAU (Gold, 718) are the highest-returning satellites over the full period, while XLE (Energy, 356) and XLF (Financials, 218) are the weakest cyclical performers, reflecting the post-2014 energy bear market and the persistent post-GFC underperformance of financials respectively.}}{2}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:price_levels}{{1}{2}{Cumulative price levels of the core and satellite assets, rebased to 100 at February 2004. Shaded regions mark the three crisis episodes inside the sample. Final index values are annotated at the right of each panel. XLK (Technology, 1471) and XAU (Gold, 718) are the highest-returning satellites over the full period, while XLE (Energy, 356) and XLF (Financials, 218) are the weakest cyclical performers, reflecting the post-2014 energy bear market and the persistent post-GFC underperformance of financials respectively}{figure.caption.1}{}}
